Aidan considers your words in silence, light gleaming off the edges of his flowing muscles as he moves from parry to attack. 

"It's suicide," he says at last, shaking his head. "Even if I slipped around its tentacles and hammered its flesh with my fists, it would rip me apart in seconds. I accept, of course. Pay me [Global: a2101_HiringAidanSitabo] shins, and my strength is yours."
{Money}

row.translation:
艾丹沉默着掂量你的话，他从格挡转入进攻，流畅肌肉的边缘泛着光。

“这是自杀，”他终于开口，摇了摇头，“就算我绕过它的触手、用拳头猛砸它的血肉，它也能在几秒内把我撕碎。不过，我接受。付我 [Global: a2101_HiringAidanSitabo] 枚希恩，我的力气就归你使。”
{Money}

patch.translation:
“如果你真是绽灵的主宰，那你也应当是自己生命的主宰。掌控你的命运，去选择……而不是任由他人摆布你。这就是权力的真谛。”

{SCRIPT:  Can collase this and the two nodes below into a single one once assets are confirmed working.}

{CRIT}

她看起来也像是正要咽下什么恶心的东西。“我感激你。”

她快步走向出口，她的打手紧随其后。

{SCRIPT: Fire a cutscene wherein the Memovira abandons her fortress with her followers (i.e., they exit and despawn).}

entry_reviews.source_excerpt:
"I am grateful that we could come to an agreement."

She takes the eggs from you, and hands you [Global: a2301_StichusEggsPeliai] shins in return.

{LOOT: PARTIAL REWARD}

He mutters. "I wouldn't be so sure of that."

{ADAM: We should check this conditional's number to make sure it's appropriate}
{COLIN: This is really just a design flag so we remember to look}

It slashes open your forearm, and you cry out, jerking your arm away. 

{SCRIPT: Damage the player.}

{DAMAGE}

As he attacks, the other soldiers join in.

{SCRIPT: Start Tussle}

{DAMAGE}

"I... don't know. The patrol schedules have been spotty lately, and we had another one go missing just the other day - " He clamps his mouth shut. The mutants leer appreciatively at this newfound alibi, and the enforcer hastily adds, "-but the Memovira spared no expense to find them."

No one believes him.

{SCRIPT:  Add a negative asset to the tasks to convince the mutants to stop. The player just inadvertently gave them an alibi to attack these guys.}

"If you are truly the ruler of the Bloom, then you should also be the mistress of your own life. Control your destiny, and choose... rather than letting others act upon you. This is the truth of power."

{SCRIPT:  Can collase this and the two nodes below into a single one once assets are confirmed working.}

{CRIT}

She also looks like she's about to swallow something disgusting. "You have my gratitude."

She walks quickly to the exit, her thugs close at her heels.

{SCRIPT: Fire a cutscene wherein the Memovira abandons her fortress with her followers (i.e., they exit and despawn).}

"We met with his agent, a graying, hirsute, overbuilt specimen with unsightly slashes of scar tissue across his brutish cheekbones." 

The automaton shakes its metal head in distaste, contrasting somewhat oddly with the fixed gaze of the severed head below. "Apologies. We find it odd that such an illustrious personage would use so unsuitable a specimen as their respresentative."

{ADAM: This node will need to be updated with Tash's description. Sharepoint doesn't have a whole lot on the guy besides "stocky", and I couldn't get anything from either version of the Kholn Village Mere.}

You lunge at the Decanted. Its hand darts to a series of rounded buttons on the front of its armored shell. 

A radiant pulse of light staggers you. When your vision clears, the creature is gone. 

{SCRIPT: B-priority, this will start a Tussle (and the RanItOff flag will get set only if the player wins).}

[This is the marker Matak was looking for. You found it. Good job.]

{SCRIPT: Matak is in party.}
{SCRIPT: Matak leaves party.}

She shuts her eyes. "There is a place called the Resonance," she intones. "A door in the deepest fathoms."

Eyes still closed, she points to a new portal that wasn't there before. "The Resonance lies through there. You must find it. *Your* body is the key. Open it. Enter it. Then you can stop the Sorrow and be free."

{ADAM: If I get permission to revise, I'd rather this say something about the player "receiving all the combined power of every castoff" or something, just so it doesn't feel so much like they're stopping the Sorrow in the Fortress and then have to do it all over again here.}
